What is a Web Worker?

A Web Worker is a JavaScript feature that allows code to run in a background thread, separate from the browser's main thread.

Normally, JavaScript runs on a single thread, which means:

UI rendering
Event handling
DOM updates
JavaScript execution

all happen on the same thread.

If a heavy computation takes a long time, the main thread gets blocked, causing the page to freeze.

Web Workers solve this problem by moving expensive tasks to a separate thread.